t I I can't  honestly say that I was impressed by it  now I felt like they did better than  2018 for the most part the only real big  battles is like the dragon you fought  the stranger a couple times and that was  pretty much it this game it is a long  game it is about 30 hours and in the 30  hours there's probably a good six maybe  seven fights and I know there's some  stuff in the side missions that I  haven't got to yet and I got to a lot of  them but as far as like the main bosses  there are some that are hit there are  some that's a miss but I feel like they  did enough here to satisfy me now if  they make another one I want them to  focus more on the boss battles because I  think what makes God of War God of War  is that Gore is that M rated Gore that  that that destroy all things Gore that  rip people to shreds Gore that boss  battle where you know you come up to  Hercules and you take his own weapons  and Bash his skull in that is what makes  God of War to me and I feel like this is  God of War but it's downplayed a lot  significantly and maybe it's a lot to do  with you know budgeting I know that some  of these big AAA battles in the type of  style that God of War is currently going  into so maybe that takes a little bit of  time but they did a decent job it's like  I said I wouldn't say it's phenomenal or  anything like that when it comes to the  story in turns there were a couple  bosses towards the end of the game that  I was a little disappointed with that I  felt like they built up anticipation to  fight them and it just wasn't caught up  what it was to be you know I think that  this is a good direction for God of War  I don't know where they're gonna go next  with this but I'm kind of curious to see  exactly what the feedback they took from  this game when they're making the next  one because like I said this is a good  game guys you know they took a lot of  the feedback that the community gave  them and there was a lot of feedback you  know there was a huge thing on the ball  since people weren't feeling that the  stranger and the dragon was like one of  the key boss fights in the original God  of War that gave us a lot more of that  like I said I would appreciate more like  phase boss fights where you change  location there was a particular one  where you fought in pretty much their  version of hell that was a really nice  boss fight I really enjoyed that I would  like I just want more of that that's all  I just want more fights and maybe it's  because they don't have access to the  amount of gods that Greek mythology had  I don't know much about North mythology  if they have the amount of gods that  Greek mythology has but they had a lot  to work with in Greek mythology when it  comes to the original God of Wars and  maybe it's because their rash these with  just two games because if you guys think  about it in the original God of Wars  they had a lot of build up time when you  got to Zeus you really wanted to kill  Zeus when you got to anyone for that  matter you saw Hercules people know who  Hercules is they knew who they were  fighting there was a lot of things they  could work with those original games  because they built up to them from their  first God of War to the second God of  War to the third God of War that's why  because of the build up from the first  two God Awards they were able to jump  straight into the third God of War just  killing Poseidon the way they did I  think that might be the biggest issue  when it comes to the story of these  newer games now the story was fantastic  I do have nitpicks on it like I said  there were things towards the end of the  game that I was not feeling too much but  as far as the overall game the game is  is is amazing it really is I I recommend  all you guys buying it's worth seventy  dollars don't wait for this game if you  have a PlayStation 4 or 5 I would  probably wait for a five uh that's  probably just me I don't know how this  game would run on the PS4